Fix a prime $p$, and let $R$ be either $MU_{(p)}$ or the Brown–Peterson spectrum $BP$ at that prime. For $k\geq1$, let $f_R(k)$ be the least integer $n\geq0$ for which $$\label{eq:nilpotence-truncated-action}
I_R^{\wedge n}\wedge\tau_{<k}\mathbb S_{(p)}
 \xrightarrow{\varphi_{R,n}\wedge\operatorname{id}}
\tau_{<k}\mathbb S_{(p)}$$ is nullhomotopic. These integers exist and satisfy $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\frac{f_R(k)}{k}=0.$$ Equivalently, $f_R(k)$ is the least $n$ such that, for every connective $p$-local spectrum $X$ and every $i<k$, a class in $\pi_iX$ of $R$-Adams filtration at least $n$ is zero.

For the finite box families in [eq:box-pairs](#eq:box-pairs), one sufficiently small collapse support gives equivalences $$\label{eq:box-duality}
 \mathcal C_\alpha(Z)\simeq
 F\left(\Sigma^\infty T_\alpha(Z),\Sigma^M\mathbb S\right).$$ They are induced by collapse around equality and are natural both under box inclusions and under inclusions of coordinate arrangements. In the box variable the cofibers are covariant and the test spaces are contravariant, by quotient collapse. In the arrangement variable, the cofibers are contravariant and the test spaces are covariant.
